### ============================================================
###  Workshop Management System — Manual Scenario Test Suite
###  Run these requests in order using the VS Code REST Client
###  extension or JetBrains HTTP Client.
###
###  Scenario Coverage:
###    Scenario 1 — Customer Check-In & Service Request Creation
###    Scenario 2 — Workshop Inspection & Quotation Generation
### ============================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5085

# -------------------------------------------------------------
# SEED DATA (replace with real IDs from your database)
# -------------------------------------------------------------
# These GUIDs must exist in your database before running the
# scenarios. Seed them via your DbContext or a migration.
# -------------------------------------------------------------
@customerId  = 3f5e1d8a-4b2c-4f6e-9a7d-1b3c5e7f9a2d
@mechanicId  = 7a2b4c6d-8e0f-4a1b-9c3d-5e7f9a1b3c5e
@vehicleId   = 1b3c5e7f-9a2d-4f6e-8b0c-2d4f6a8c0e2f

# After running Scenario 1, copy the returned `id` field here:
@serviceRequestId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000


### ============================================================
###  SCENARIO 1 — Customer Check-In / Service Request Creation
### ============================================================
#
#  Business Context:
#    A customer arrives at the reception desk with their vehicle.
#    The front-desk operator logs a Repair service request.
#    The system uses the Factory Pattern to instantiate a
#    RepairRequest entity and persists it with a status of "Open".
#
#  Expected Result:
#    HTTP 201 Created
#    Body contains: { id, requestType, status, customerId, ... }
#
#  Endpoint: POST /api/Reception/create
#  Controller: ReceptionController
#  Handler:   CreateServiceRequestCommandHandler
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Reception/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requestType": 0,
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "mechanicId": "{{mechanicId}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{vehicleId}}",
  "price": 850.00,
  "commissionType": 1,
  "commissionValue": 10,
  "description": "Customer reports engine overheating and a knocking sound at idle. Full diagnostic and repair required."
}

###
# NOTE: Copy the `id` from the 201 response above and paste it
# into the @serviceRequestId variable at the top of this file
# before running Scenario 2.
###


### ============================================================
###  SCENARIO 2 — Workshop Inspection & Quotation Generation
### ============================================================
#
#  Business Context:
#    The assigned mechanic inspects the vehicle and identifies
#    the required parts and labour. They generate a formal
#    quotation for the customer's approval.
#
#    The system:
#      1. Retrieves the existing ServiceRequest.
#      2. Creates a Quotation with the provided line items.
#      3. Calculates each item's TotalPrice = Quantity × UnitPrice.
#      4. Transitions the ServiceRequest status to
#         "PendingCustomerApproval".
#      5. Returns the new Quotation ID and grand total.
#
#  Expected Result:
#    HTTP 201 Created
#    Body contains: { quotationId, grandTotal, serviceRequestId, ... }
#
#  Endpoint: POST /api/requests/{id}/quotations
#  Controller: OperationsController
#  Handler:   GenerateQuotationCommandHandler
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/{{serviceRequestId}}/quotations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    {
      "type": 0,
      "description": "Radiator Cap",
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": 45.00
    },
    {
      "type": 0,
      "description": "Coolant (5 Litre)",
      "quantity": 2,
      "unitPrice": 75.00
    },
    {
      "type": 0,
      "description": "Serpentine Belt",
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": 120.00
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "description": "Engine Cooling System Flush & Refill",
      "quantity": 2,
      "unitPrice": 95.00
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "description": "Engine Idle Diagnostic & Timing Check",
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": 150.00
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Radiator cap was holding pressure at 12 psi (below spec). Belt showed visible cracking. Full coolant system flush recommended every 40,000 km thereafter."
}

### ============================================================
###  END OF SCENARIO TEST SUITE
### ============================================================
#
#  QuotationItemType enum values:
#    0 = Part   (physical spare part)
#    1 = Labor  (workshop labour hours)
#
#  RequestType enum values:
#    0 = Repair
#    1 = PurchaseOnly
#    2 = InspectionOnly
#
#  CommissionType enum values:
#    0 = Fixed      (flat monetary amount)
#    1 = Percentage (% of total price)
#
### ============================================================

### ============================================================
###  SCENARIO 3 — Customer Approval / Rejection
### ============================================================

# After running Scenario 2, copy the returned `quotationId` here:
@quotationId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# Endpoint: POST /api/Quotations/{id}/approve
# Expected Result: 200 OK
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Quotations/{{quotationId}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

###

# Endpoint: POST /api/Quotations/{id}/reject
# Expected Result: 200 OK
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Quotations/{{quotationId}}/reject
Content-Type: application/json


### ============================================================
###  SCENARIO 4 — Repair Execution & Status Tracking
### ============================================================
#
#  Business Context:
#    The mechanic starts repairing the vehicle and needs to 
#    update the repair status to reflect real-time progress.
#
#  Endpoint: PATCH /api/requests/{id}/status
#  Controller: OperationsController
#  Handler:   UpdateServiceRequestStatusCommandHandler
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Update Status to Waiting_For_Parts (value: 8)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/{{serviceRequestId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newStatus": 8,
  "notes": "Radiator cap is out of stock. Waiting for supplier delivery tomorrow morning."
}


### ============================================================
###  SCENARIO 5 — Quality Control (QC)
### ============================================================
#
#  Business Context:
#    The mechanic completes work, status is set to Ready_For_QC (10).
#    A supervisor inspects the vehicle. It first fails due to a note,
#    then passes and progresses to Ready_For_Invoicing (12).
#
#  Endpoint: POST /api/requests/{id}/qc
#  Controller: OperationsController
#  Handler:   PerformQCCommandHandler
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# First, transition the request to Ready_For_QC (10) manually
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/{{serviceRequestId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newStatus": 10,
  "notes": "All parts installed, vehicle is ready for final quality control."
}

###

# Second, fail the QC inspection
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/{{serviceRequestId}}/qc
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isPassed": false,
  "notes": "Coolant cap is not properly tightened. Send back to mechanic."
}

###

# Third, transition it back to Ready_For_QC manually (after fixing the issue)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/{{serviceRequestId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newStatus": 10,
  "notes": "Tightened coolant cap. Ready for QC again."
}

###

# Fourth, pass the QC inspection
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/{{serviceRequestId}}/qc
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isPassed": true,
  "notes": "Pressure holding steady. Engine sounds good. Ready for billing."
}

### ============================================================
###  SCENARIO 6 — Invoicing & Payment
### ============================================================
#
#  Business Context:
#    The QC has passed, and the vehicle is 'Ready_For_Invoicing'.
#    We will now generate the final invoice, transition the status
#    to 'Pending_Payment', and proceed to pay the invoice in full.
#
#  Endpoint: POST /api/requests/{id}/invoice
#  Controller: BillingController
#  Handler:   GenerateInvoiceCommandHandler
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Generate the invoice for the service request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/{{serviceRequestId}}/invoice
Content-Type: application/json

###
# NOTE: Copy the `invoiceId` from the 200 OK response above
# and paste it into the @invoiceId variable below to process payment
###

@invoiceId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# Endpoint: POST /api/invoices/{id}/pay
# Controller: BillingController
# Handler:   ProcessPaymentCommandHandler
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Pay the generated invoice in full (change amount to match total amount)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/pay
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 1000.00,
  "paymentMethod": 1,
  "transactionReference": "TXN_CARD_0991823"
}

###
# Endpoint: POST /api/requests/{id}/release
# Controller: ReceptionController
# Handler:   CloseServiceRequestCommandHandler
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Release the vehicle and calculate mechanic commission
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/{{serviceRequestId}}/release
Content-Type: application/json

### ==========================================================
### PHASE 10: SAD PATHS - HTTP TESTING (VALIDATION & BUSINESS RULES)
### ==========================================================

### SAD PATH: Invalid Service Request (Validation Error)
# Expected: 400 Bad Request with Validation Problem Details
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reception/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requestType": 0,
  "vehicleId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "customerId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "workerId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "price": -100,
  "date": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### SAD PATH: Invalid Quotation (Negative Quantity)
# Expected: 400 Bad Request with Validation Problem Details
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/operations/requests/{{serviceRequestId}}/quotations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    {
      "type": 0,
      "description": "Oil Filter",
      "quantity": -5,
      "unitPrice": 15.0
    }
  ]
}

###

### SAD PATH: Reject ALREADY Approved Quotation (Business Logic Error)
# Expected: 400 Bad Request or 409 Conflict with 'Cannot reject an already approved quotation'
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/operations/quotations/{{quotationId}}/reject
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Change of mind"
}

###

### SAD PATH: Release a Vehicle before it's Ready (Business Logic Error)
# Expected: 400 Bad Request or 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reception/requests/{{serviceRequestId}}/release
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###

### ==========================================================
### PHASE 13: WORKSHOP BOARD QUERIES (READ OPERATIONS)
### ==========================================================

### GET Paged Service Requests (Workshop Board)
# Expected: 200 OK with PagedResponse format
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/requests?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10
Accept: application/json

###

### GET Paged Service Requests (Filtered by Status, e.g. Open = 0)
# Expected: 200 OK with PagedResponse format
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/requests?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10&status=0
Accept: application/json

###

### GET Service Request Details By ID
# Expected: 200 OK with full details (Vehicle, Customer, Quotation, Invoice, StatusHistory)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/{{serviceRequestId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### ==========================================================
### PHASE 16: FINANCE & WORKERS MODULE
### ==========================================================

### GET Invoice Details By ID
# Expected: 200 OK with full details (Payments, Service Request, Quotation)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{invoiceId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### GET Worker Commissions
# Expected: 200 OK with PagedResponse format
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/{{mechanicId}}/commissions?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10
Accept: application/json

